\\f0\\b \\cf2 \\cb3 \\strokec2 ### `notebooks/model_validation_notebook.ipynb`\
\\f1\\b0 \\cf4 \\cb1 \\strokec4 \\\
\\\
\\pard\\pardeftab720\\partightenfactor0\
\\cf4 \\cb3 The analytical core. Cells are ordered as a pipeline:\\cb1 \\\
\\\
\\pard\\pardeftab720\\partightenfactor0\
\\cf5 \\cb3 \\strokec5 1.\\cf4 \\strokec4  \
\\f0\\b \\cf6 \\strokec6 **Load**\
\\f1\\b0 \\cf4 \\strokec4  - reads the Excel workbook into a pandas DataFrame.\\cb1 \\\
\\cf5 \\cb3 \\strokec5 2.\\cf4 \\strokec4  \
\\f0\\b \\cf6 \\strokec6 **Clean**\
\\f1\\b0 \\cf4 \\strokec4  - coerces placeholder strings to \\cf2 \\strokec2 `NaN`\\cf4 \\strokec4 ; drops rows null across all human/AI\\cb1 \\\
\\pard\\pardeftab720\\partightenfactor0\
\\cf4 \\cb3    annotation columns (not a blanket \\cf2 \\strokec2 `dropna`\\cf4 \\strokec4 ).\\cb1 \\\
\\pard\\pardeftab720\\partightenfactor0\
\\cf5 \\cb3 \\strokec5 3.\\cf4 \\strokec4  \
\\f0\\b \\cf6 \\strokec6 **Per-element metrics**\
\\f1\\b0 \\cf4 \\strokec4  - computes accuracy proportions for each of 14 clinical elements.\\cb1 \\\
\\cf5 \\cb3 \\strokec5 4.\\cf4 \\strokec4  \
\\f0\\b \\cf6 \\strokec6 **Hypothesis tests**\
\\f1\\b0 \\cf4 \\strokec4  - McNemar's test (exact for small n) + Agresti-Coull 95% CIs.\\cb1 \\\
\\cf5 \\cb3 \\strokec5 5.\\cf4 \\strokec4  \
\\f0\\b \\cf6 \\strokec6 **Tables/plots**\
\\f1\\b0 \\cf4 \\strokec4  - \\cf2 \\strokec2 `great_tables`\\cf4 \\strokec4  summary table and seaborn grouped bar chart.\\cb1 \\\
\\cf5 \\cb3 \\strokec5 6.\\cf4 \\strokec4  \
\\f0\\b \\cf6 \\strokec6 **Export**\
\\f1\\b0 \\cf4 \\strokec4  - writes CSV, HTML, and PNG outputs to \\cf2 \\strokec2 `outputs/`\\cf4 \\strokec4 .\\cb1 \\\
\\\
\\pard\\pardeftab720\\partightenfactor0\
\\cf4 \\cb3 The notebook also contains headed sections for stratified analysis (radiologic vs.\\cb1 \\\
\\cb3 pathologic elements; case complexity) that are placeholder headers only - no stratified\\cb1 \\\
\\cb3 computation is implemented yet.\\cb1 \\\
\\\
